00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:18.520
Your music and lyrics
deal with dark subjects

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:22.620
while also feeling rhythmical
and emotionally intelligent.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:27.930
How do you achieve that balance
between lyrics and sound?

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:33.250
Could you tell us about your songwriting?

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.010
I see.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:39.190
The balance between lyrics and sound?

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:44.470
But the lyrics and sound
are always the same, aren't they?

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:51.660
There's that new song
we recorded the other day.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:19:01.170
The lyrics are really dark,
but the sound is really bright?

00:19:01.770 --> 00:19:04.530
We decided to make it brighter.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:10.690
I feel like the lyrics
and music usually match.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:13.390
They do. When we play
according to how we feel,

00:19:13.390 --> 00:19:18.240
the energy level ends up being the same.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:19.130
Yeah.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:30.550
I always start by writing
the lyrics and music together.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:37.480
Even if I haven't written
the whole song yet,

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:42.210
I can't write unless I know what I want
to say, so I always have a general vision.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:54.050
Sometimes I include
realizations I have along the way.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:20:03.430
But even if the lyrics and music are
opposites, I have a vision from the start,

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:08.810
so I think about
how to convey that as I write.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:14.300
Although recently, I don't even do that.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.050
Yeah.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:21.530
I figure it out as I go along.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:27.750
These days I start by creating
an arrangement in the rehearsal studio,

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:33.820
and take that the recording studio
where I fine tune.

